  "verified_unaffected_boundaries": [
    "FrameBuffer requires one bounded 4..MAX_PACKET body and fragments no larger than wanted/65536; bad header is refused after only its original four bytes, before body allocation. Complete frame is retained before taking buffer and before semantic handle.",
    "Static constructor requires exact reviewed controllerV2, CallbackSnapshotConnection, actual socket and empty old peer buffer, followed by live ownership check. Actual successful construction was not exercised.",
    "Actual recv socket.timeout preserves the same fragments for continuation. EOF and OSError stop and retain partial bytes and independent transport status; EOF is not recorded as process termination.",
    "Complete-frame retention failure stops and preserves the original complete buffer without calling handle. Semantic refusal after retention also stops, with original frame already in custody. Adapter/controller duplicate frame retention is explicit and remains subject to existing aggregate custody limits."
  ],
